  {journeyIds:['LJ-08'],testId:'learning-history-page',scope:'30k synthetic scalar history projections exercise public paged history counts, cursor ordering, languages, calendar filters, invalid/future ranges and DST in SQLite/Wasm against complete-record selection. Summary groups remain language-specific; only bounded record JSON is decoded, not Target/Run/Event facts. Projection shape/parity, not manufactured learning outcomes, browser timezone or OPFS latency.'},
  {journeyIds:['LJ-08'],testId:'runtime-learning-candidates',scope:'SQLite/Wasm scalar scheduling index matches the complete pure queue on 10k synthetic projection inputs, including current/Retry exclusions, policy readiness, pinned language pair, daily quota and next-change timing. Worker result is bounded to candidate prefixes plus exact retries; no Target/material JSON decode on continuation or unchanged index open. Projection shape/parity, not genuine learning history or OPFS latency.'},
  {journeyIds:['LJ-08'],testId:'learning-command-receipt',scope:'Production Learning commands persist bounded receipts rather than duplicate Run/material payloads. Exact original metadata replays after later progress without resubmission; altered input conflicts. Restore and live replay reject a receipt pointing at another genuine Run for the same Target or a changed context/intent/time. Controlled storage, not Chromium/OPFS latency.'},
  {journeyIds:['LJ-08'],testId:'learning-material-pins',scope:'Formal actions at different instants share exact immutable bodies. Actual v1/v2/v3 unacted refreshes and same-instant Again/reveal/completion replay by continuous Action/lifecycle Run revisions without public cache or device receipts. Saved protocol Steps cite acted material, first-binding order survives sorted encoding, and missing/duplicate/gapped causal witnesses, reordered refreshes, future next material and unreferenced bodies reject. A start before actual local source admission rejects without writes; correctly rehashed pins cannot erase Ready or move it before admission/after Run start. Controlled storage; no capacity, external publisher trust or latency verdict.'},
  {journeyIds:['LJ-08'],testId:'learning-management-query',scope:'Actual initial completion, Again Review and Relearning over SQLite/Wasm produce compact Study records identical to the full projection without hydrating Target/Run/Event payloads. Unfinished initial Again has no completion record; a formal failed Review remains a Review attempt. An index write failure rolls back facts and receipts. Missing local tables/indexes rebuild from unchanged facts and read errors fail closed. Not an OPFS/UI latency claim.'},
  {journeyIds:['LJ-08'],testId:'retention-review-capacity',scope:'Specialized isolated Chromium/OPFS baseline with actual Initial Completion and due Review history generated through LearningSystem commands over SQLite/Wasm, fully replay-validated by the Node producer before digest-checked bounded fixture copying. Measures actual UI reveal, rating-to-next-target, Study, statistics, history-to-correct-Target and reload separately from setup cost; management/history/Target read failures hide stale facts and explicit retry restores actual records. Pagination and type filters retain full-range counts. Fixture copying is not product backup restore. Configurable Target count, synthetic low-media source, 1x CPU; registration is not a passing capacity or audio-quality verdict.'},
  {journeyIds:['LJ-08'],testId:'library-transaction-and-replay',scope:'Actual SQLite/Wasm kernel in Node: supplied crossday clock selects superseded introductions through indexed date ranges and active due targets through Route indexes. Synthetic 10k already-retained compact scheduling rows (5k due) exercise Home planning with a 1500ms regression ceiling, no materials/history returned. Zero history Runs: not Chromium/OPFS latency, genuine completion history, review settlement or a full user-performance verdict.'},
  {journeyIds:['LJ-08'],testId:'review-session',scope:'Production Learning interface with actual Portable admission and a controlled Library adapter: review-only selects genuine due work instead of a paused initial Run, persists its intent across continuation, preserves the original Step, and finishes before new learning. Hard/Again remain canonical grades; exact replay and stale revision protect one Review settlement, distinct Relearning does not reschedule again. Backup validation without public artifact cache replays lightweight history and rejects altered memory revisions/grades. Future command timestamps and review-only initial work reject without writes; explicit three-member Book enrollment and quantity change create no initial eligibility during review-only. Adapter contract rejects intent/language mutation. Not shipped UI, OPFS latency, long-history capacity or external-provider evidence.'},
